    54	// The MHPCO settles a damage only against an item the policy actually covers,
    55	// so it refuses a damage entry naming anything else -- and the whole claim with
    56	// it. A damage entry names only the type of the item it befell, so the MHPCO
    57	// identifies the covering item no further than the policy's first insured item
    58	// of that type. Where a policy covers several alike items this is a deliberate
    59	// approximation: alike items share the traits the reimbursement clauses read,
    60	// so any of them yields the same clause. Counting damage entries against the
    61	// insured items of their type -- and refusing an excess -- is a further
    62	// condition of coverage the MHPCO has not yet put into force.
    63	function firstInsuredItemCoveringDamage(policy: Policy, damage: Damage): Item {
    64	  const insured = policy.insuredItems.find(
    65	    (item) => item.type === damage.itemType,
    66	  );
